    "created_at": "2025-05-01T06:48:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-01T06:48:14Z",
    "body": "I think that's somewhat separable. Subresource requests will generally have clients. Null client cases are rarer, and will generally come from \"background-ish\" features like [FedCM](https://w3c-fedid.github.io/FedCM/#send-a-disconnect-request), [Private Aggregation](https://patcg-individual-drafts.github.io/private-aggregation-api/#create-a-report-request), [Background Fetch](https://wicg.github.io/background-fetch/#dom-backgroundfetchmanager-fetch).\r\n\r\nProbably all of those can suppress the user prompts and just fail.",
